<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Apple requires a privacy manifest for the app, and separately one from each
  SDK it embeds. This file covers THIS app's own binary only: the Flutter engine
  and every plugin used here (flutter_secure_storage, url_launcher, share_plus,
  path_provider) ship their own manifests, and Xcode collects them into the
  privacy report at archive time.

  NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes is empty on purpose: the app's own code calls none of
  the APIs on Apple's required-reason list. It keeps the session in the Keychain
  (flutter_secure_storage), not in UserDefaults, and reads no file timestamps,
  disk space or boot time of its own. If that changes, the reason code belongs
  here, and a wrong or missing entry is rejected at upload.

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty because nothing is collected BY US: the
  app talks only to the mail server the person signs in to, which is theirs or
  their operator's, and there is no analytics, advertising or crash SDK in it
  (see pubspec.yaml). What that server stores is that server's business, and is
  covered by its own privacy policy — but the App Store privacy questionnaire is
  answered by the publisher, not by this file, so check it agrees with this.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>

	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
